    "narrative": "The run found a mixed picture: it did not support the idea that net margin had deteriorated over recent periods, but it did support the idea that revenue growth had increased and could explain the margin change. So the evidence points more toward revenue growth as the explanation than toward a clear deterioration in margin quality.\n\nThe margin-deterioration claim was rejected, with more refuting evidence than supporting evidence. The revenue-growth claim was supported, with several pieces of evidence in its favor and none against it. Overall, the run tested two hypotheses and ended with one supported claim.\n\nIt used repeated trend-break analyses, time-series trend checks, change-point detection, and a distribution summary before stopping because it had enough evidence. What remains open is whether any margin decline was sustained rather than a one-off fluctuation, whether the timing of revenue growth lines up with the margin movement, and whether the revenue-growth explanation can be made stronger.",
    "statement": "Supported: Revenue growth has increased over recent periods at these companies and could explain the margin change. | Not supported: Net margin has deteriorated over recent periods at these companies.",
